            {
                "entry_id": "f4ce55d9-b688-30d2-bf8d-b1890167bafc",
                "word": "moneymaker",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "90bd780f-086f-4308-bd8f-e65555ff5f78",
                        "entry_id": "f4ce55d9-b688-30d2-bf8d-b1890167bafc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "moneymakers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "995484af-a6b0-367a-88c2-5546412daebb",
                        "entry_id": "f4ce55d9-b688-30d2-bf8d-b1890167bafc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that earns or makes money; anything lucrative or profitable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "239710b4-884c-47cd-9760-c8255e35db9e",
                                "sense_id": "995484af-a6b0-367a-88c2-5546412daebb",
                                "text": "With careful management, she hoped to grow her small business into a real moneymaker."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b978de75-6e4e-4e38-b0fc-44a18b345344",
                                "sense_id": "995484af-a6b0-367a-88c2-5546412daebb",
                                "text": "“The media don’t really give young people role models anymore,” says Christina Chinn, 21, of Denver. “Now you get role models like Donald Trump and all of the moneymakers — no one with real ideals.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ae2d7f2-07c6-40f0-9f02-2032df62674b",
                                "sense_id": "995484af-a6b0-367a-88c2-5546412daebb",
                                "text": "School lunch as a moneymaker is not possible in most public schools because the federal National School Lunch Program that provides subsidies to feed low-income students specifically prohibits it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "494e392e-1306-4817-b858-5708fb65b115",
                                "sense_id": "995484af-a6b0-367a-88c2-5546412daebb",
                                "text": "In a sense, The Bleeding Edge is about the privatization of our well-being; our bodies and illnesses are money-makers and, even if we know that our doctors have our best interests in mind, a treatment is some way a transaction between a patient and a glacially huge pharma-medical conglomerate out to make a profit."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cbfa7689-d534-3d9b-8142-6ded668df082",
                        "entry_id": "f4ce55d9-b688-30d2-bf8d-b1890167bafc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "(usually a woman's) butt, ass, rear end"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang",
                            "vulgar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d21de3f-d643-48b5-8a54-8f07f87ae1d2",
                                "sense_id": "cbfa7689-d534-3d9b-8142-6ded668df082",
                                "text": "Shake your moneymaker / You gotta shake your moneymaker / And then?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fab2ff7f-4b6d-32f4-b5f3-315932632a83",
                        "entry_id": "f4ce55d9-b688-30d2-bf8d-b1890167bafc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A lady’s breast."
